(                                PREFACE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_This book is written to offer a simple and natural explanation of one) Tj T*
(of the most common and most perplexing problems of human life,?a problem) Tj T*
(which presents itself to almost every individual for practical solution,) Tj T*
(and which demands the most serious attention of the moralist, the) Tj T*
(physician, and the sociologist_?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_To show how some of the worst evils under which we suffer, evils long) Tj T*
(supposed to be inherent and ineradicable in our natures, are but the) Tj T*
(result of certain arbitrary conditions of our own adoption, and how, by) Tj T*
(removing those conditions, we may remove the evils resultant_?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_To point out how far we have already gone in the path of improvement,) Tj T*
(and how irresistibly the social forces of to-day are compelling us) Tj T*
(further, even without our knowledge and against our violent) Tj T*
(opposition,?an advance which may be greatly quickened by our recognition) Tj T*
(and assistance_?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_To reach in especial the thinking women of to-day, and urge upon them a) Tj T*
(new sense, not only of their social responsibility as individuals, but) Tj T*
