(Since we have learned to study the development of human life as we study) Tj T*
(the evolution of species throughout the animal kingdom, some peculiar) Tj T*
(phenomena which have puzzled the philosopher and moralist for so long,) Tj T*
(begin to show themselves in a new light. We begin to see that, so far) Tj T*
(from being inscrutable problems, requiring another life to explain,) Tj T*
(these sorrows and perplexities of our lives are but the natural results) Tj T*
(of natural causes, and that, as soon as we ascertain the causes, we can) Tj T*
(do much to remove them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In spite of the power of the individual will to struggle against) Tj T*
(conditions, to resist them for a while, and sometimes to overcome them,) Tj T*
(it remains true that the human creature is affected by his environment,) Tj T*
(as is every other living thing. The power of the individual will to) Tj T*
