(Christendom?united at least in this most unchristian deed?the Jew was) Tj T*
(forced to get his livelihood by commercial methods solely. Many effects) Tj T*
(can be traced in him to the fierce pressure of the social conditions to) Tj T*
(which he was subjected: the intense family devotion of a people who had) Tj T*
(no country, no king, no room for joy and pride except the family; the) Tj T*
(reduced size and tremendous vitality and endurance of the pitilessly) Tj T*
(selected survivors of the Ghetto; the repeated bursts of erratic genius) Tj T*
(from the human spirit so inhumanly restrained. But more patent still is) Tj T*
(the effect of the economic conditions,?the artificial development of a) Tj T*
(race of traders and dealers in money, from the lowest pawnbroker to the) Tj T*
(house of Rothschild; a special kind of people, bred of the economic) Tj T*
(environment in which they were compelled to live.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One rough but familiar instance of the same effect, from the same cause,) Tj T*
(we can all see in the marked distinction between the pastoral, the) Tj T*
(agricultural, and the manufacturing classes in any nation, though their) Tj T*
(other conditions be the same. On the clear line of argument that) Tj T*
(functions and organs are developed by use, that what we use most is) Tj T*
(developed most, and that the daily processes of supplying economic needs) Tj T*
(are the processes that we most use, it follows that, when we find) Tj T*
(special economic conditions affecting any special class of people, we) Tj T*
(may look for special results, and find them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In view of these facts, attention is now called to a certain marked and) Tj T*
(peculiar economic condition affecting the human race, and unparalleled) Tj T*
(in the organic world. We are the only animal species in which the female) Tj T*
(depends on the male for food, the only animal species in which the) Tj T*
(sex-relation is also an economic relation. With us an entire sex lives) Tj T*
(in a relation of economic dependence upon the other sex, and the) Tj T*
(economic relation is combined with the sex-relation. The economic status) Tj T*
(of the human female is relative to the sex-relation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is commonly assumed that this condition also obtains among other) Tj T*
(animals, but such is not the case. There are many birds among which,) Tj T*
(during the nesting season, the male helps the female feed the young, and) Tj T*
(partially feeds her; and, with certain of the higher carnivora, the male) Tj T*
(helps the female feed the young, and partially feeds her. In no case) Tj T*
(does she depend on him absolutely, even during this season, save in that) Tj T*
(of the hornbill, where the female, sitting on her nest in a hollow tree,) Tj T*
(is walled in with clay by the male, so that only her beak projects; and) Tj T*
(then he feeds her while the eggs are developing. But even the female) Tj T*
(hornbill does not expect to be fed at any other time. The female bee and) Tj T*
(ant are economically dependent, but not on the male. The workers are) Tj T*
(females, too, specialized to economic functions solely. And with the) Tj T*
(carnivora, if the young are to lose one parent, it might far better be) Tj T*
(the father: the mother is quite competent to take care of them herself.) Tj T*
(With many species, as in the case of the common cat, she not only feeds) Tj T*
(herself and her young, but has to defend the young against the male as) Tj T*
(well. In no case is the female throughout her life supported by the) Tj T*
(male.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the human species the condition is permanent and general, though) Tj T*
