(there are exceptions, and though the present century is witnessing the) Tj T*
(beginnings of a great change in this respect. We have not been) Tj T*
(accustomed to face this fact beyond our loose generalization that it was) Tj T*
(?natural,? and that other animals did so, too.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To many this view will not seem clear at first; and the case of working) Tj T*
(peasant women or females of savage tribes, and the general household) Tj T*
(industry of women, will be instanced against it. Some careful and honest) Tj T*
(discrimination is needed to make plain to ourselves the essential facts) Tj T*
(of the relation, even in these cases. The horse, in his free natural) Tj T*
(condition, is economically independent. He gets his living by his own) Tj T*
(exertions, irrespective of any other creature. The horse, in his present) Tj T*
(condition of slavery, is economically dependent. He gets his living at) Tj T*
(the hands of his master; and his exertions, though strenuous, bear no) Tj T*
(direct relation to his living. In fact, the horses who are the best fed) Tj T*
(and cared for and the horses who are the hardest worked are quite) Tj T*
(different animals. The horse works, it is true; but what he gets to eat) Tj T*
(depends on the power and will of his master. His living comes through) Tj T*
(another. He is economically dependent. So with the hard-worked savage or) Tj T*
(peasant women. Their labor is the property of another: they work under) Tj T*
(another will; and what they receive depends not on their labor, but on) Tj T*
(the power and will of another. They are economically dependent. This is) Tj T*
(true of the human female both individually and collectively.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In studying the economic position of the sexes collectively, the) Tj T*
(difference is most marked. As a social animal, the economic status of) Tj T*
(man rests on the combined and exchanged services of vast numbers of) Tj T*
(progressively specialized individuals. The economic progress of the) Tj T*
(race, its maintenance at any period, its continued advance, involve the) Tj T*
(collective activities of all the trades, crafts, arts, manufactures,) Tj T*
(inventions, discoveries, and all the civil and military institutions) Tj T*
(that go to maintain them. The economic status of any race at any time,) Tj T*
(with its involved effect on all the constituent individuals, depends on) Tj T*
(their world-wide labors and their free exchange. Economic progress,) Tj T*
(however, is almost exclusively masculine. Such economic processes as) Tj T*
(women have been allowed to exercise are of the earliest and most) Tj T*
(primitive kind. Were men to perform no economic services save such as) Tj T*
(are still performed by women, our racial status in economics would be) Tj T*
(reduced to most painful limitations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To take from any community its male workers would paralyze it) Tj T*
(economically to a far greater degree than to remove its female workers.) Tj T*
(The labor now performed by the women could be performed by the men,) Tj T*
(requiring only the setting back of many advanced workers into earlier) Tj T*
(forms of industry; but the labor now performed by the men could not be) Tj T*
(performed by the women without generations of effort and adaptation. Men) Tj T*
(can cook, clean, and sew as well as women; but the making and managing) Tj T*
(of the great engines of modern industry, the threading of earth and sea) Tj T*
(in our vast systems of transportation, the handling of our elaborate) Tj T*
(machinery of trade, commerce, government,?these things could not be done) Tj T*
(so well by women in their present degree of economic development.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
