(with the ties of blood, woman was cut off from personal activity in) Tj T*
(social economics, and confined to the functional activities of her sex.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In keeping her on this primitive basis of economic life, we have kept) Tj T*
(half humanity tied to the starting-post, while the other half ran. We) Tj T*
(have trained and bred one kind of qualities into one-half the species,) Tj T*
(and another kind into the other half. And then we wonder at the) Tj T*
(contradictions of human nature! For instance, we have done all we could,) Tj T*
(in addition to natural forces, to make men brave. We have done all we) Tj T*
(could, in addition to natural forces, to make women cowards. And, since) Tj T*
(every human creature is born of two parents, it is not surprising that) Tj T*
(we are a little mixed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have trained in men the large qualities of social usefulness which) Tj T*
(the pressure of their economic conditions was also developing; and we) Tj T*
(have done this by means of conscious praise and blame, reward and) Tj T*
(punishment, and with the aid of law and custom. We have trained in) Tj T*
(women, by the same means, the small qualities of personal usefulness) Tj T*
(which the pressure of their economic conditions was also developing. We) Tj T*
(have made a creature who is not homogeneous, whose life is fed by two) Tj T*
(currents of inheritance as dissimilar and opposed as could be well) Tj T*
(imagined. We have bred a race of psychic hybrids, and the moral) Tj T*
(qualities of hybrids are well known.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Away back in that early beginning, by dividing the economic conditions) Tj T*
(of women and men, we have divided their psychic development, and built) Tj T*
(into the constitution of the race the irreconcilable elements of these) Tj T*
(diverse characters. The incongruous behavior of this cross-bred product) Tj T*
(is the riddle of human life. We ourselves, by maintaining this) Tj T*
(artificial diversity between the sexes, have constantly kept before us) Tj T*
(the enigma which we found so hard to solve, and have preserved in our) Tj T*
(own characters the confusion and contradiction which is our greatest) Tj T*
(difficulty in life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The largest and most radical effect of restoring women to economic) Tj T*
(independence will be in its result in clarifying and harmonizing the) Tj T*
(human soul. With a homogeneous nature bred of two parents in the same) Tj T*
(degree of social development, we shall be able to feel simply, to see) Tj T*
(clearly, to agree with ourselves, to be one person and master of our own) Tj T*
(lives, instead of wrestling in such hopeless perplexity with what we) Tj T*
(have called ?man?s dual nature.? Marry a civilized man to a primitive) Tj T*
(savage, and their child will naturally have a dual nature. Marry an) Tj T*
(Anglo-Saxon to an African or Oriental, and their child has a dual) Tj T*
ET
