stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(nature. Marry any man of a highly developed nation, full of the) Tj T*
(specialized activities of his race and their accompanying moral) Tj T*
(qualities, to the carefully preserved, rudimentary female creature he) Tj T*
(has so religiously maintained by his side, and you have as result what) Tj T*
(we all know so well,?the human soul in its pitiful, well-meaning) Tj T*
(efforts, its cross-eyed, purblind errors, its baby fits of passion, and) Tj T*
(its beautiful and ceaseless upward impulse through all this wavering.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We are quite familiar with this result, but we have not so far) Tj T*
(accurately located the cause. We have had our glimmering perception that) Tj T*
(woman had something to do with it; and she has been treated accordingly,) Tj T*
(by many simple races, to her further injury, and to that of the whole) Tj T*
(people. What we need to see is that it is not woman as a sex who is) Tj T*
(responsible for this mis-mothered world, but the economic position of) Tj T*
(woman which makes her what she is. If men were so placed, it would have) Tj T*
(the same effect. Not the sex-relation, but the economic relation of the) Tj T*
(sexes, has so tangled the skein of human life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Besides the essential evils of an unbalanced nature, many harmful) Tj T*
(qualities have been developed in human characters by these conditions.) Tj T*
(For countless centuries we have sought to develope, by selection and) Tj T*
(education, a timid submission in woman. When there did appear ?a curst) Tj T*
(shrew,? she was left unmarried; and her temper perished with her, or she) Tj T*
(was ?tamed? by some Petruchio. The dependence of women on the personal) Tj T*
(favor of men has produced an exceeding cleverness in the adaptation of) Tj T*
(the dependent one to the source of her supplies. Under the necessity of) Tj T*
(pleasing, whether she wished or no, of interceding for a child?s pardon) Tj T*
(or of suing for new pleasures for herself, ?the vices of the slave? have) Tj T*
(been forever maintained in this housemaid of the world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another discord introduced by the condition of servitude is that between) Tj T*
(will and action. A servant places his time and strength at the disposal) Tj T*
(of another will. He must hold himself in readiness to do what he is) Tj T*
(told; and the mere physical law of conservation of energy, to say) Tj T*
(nothing of his own conscious judgment, forbids wasting nerve-force in) Tj T*
(planning and undertaking what he may not be able to accomplish. This) Tj T*
(produces a condition of inactivity, save under compulsion, and, on the) Tj T*
(other side, a perverse, capricious wilfulness in little things,?the) Tj T*
(reaction from a forced submission.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A more insidious, disintegrating force to offset the evolution of human) Tj T*
(character could hardly be imagined than this steady training of the) Tj T*
(habits of servitude into half the human race,?the mother of all of it.) Tj T*
(These results have been modified, of course, by the different education) Tj T*
(and environment of men, developing in them opposite qualities, and) Tj T*
(transmitting the contradictory traits to the children indiscriminately.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Heredity has no Salic law. The boy inherits from his mother, as well as) Tj T*
(from his father; the girl from her father, as well as from her mother.) Tj T*
(This has prevented the full evil of the results that plight have ensued,) Tj T*
(but has also added to the personal difficulties of each of us, and) Tj T*
(retarded the general progress of the race.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
