() Tj T*
(Worse than the check set upon the physical activities of women has been) Tj T*
(the restriction of their power to think and judge for themselves. The) Tj T*
(extended use of the human will and its decisions is conditioned upon) Tj T*
(free, voluntary action. In her rudimentary position, woman was denied) Tj T*
(the physical freedom which underlies all knowledge, she was denied the) Tj T*
(mental freedom which is the path to further wisdom, she was denied the) Tj T*
(moral freedom of being mistress of her own action and of learning by the) Tj T*
(merciful law of consequences what was right and what was wrong; and she) Tj T*
(has remained, perforce, undeveloped in the larger judgment of ethics.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Her moral sense is large enough, morbidly large, because in this) Tj T*
(tutelage she is always being praised or blamed for her conduct. She) Tj T*
(lives in a forcing-bed of sensitiveness to moral distinctions, but the) Tj T*
(broad judgment that alone can guide and govern this sensitiveness she) Tj T*
(has not. Her contribution to moral progress has added to the anguish of) Tj T*
(the world the fierce sense of sin and shame, the desperate desire to do) Tj T*
(right, the fear of wrong; without giving it the essential help of a) Tj T*
(practical wisdom and a regulated will. Inheriting with each generation) Tj T*
(the accumulating forces of our social nature, set back in each) Tj T*
(generation by the conditions of the primitive human female, women have) Tj T*
(become vividly self-conscious centres of moral impulse, but poor guides) Tj T*
(as to the conduct which alone can make that impulse useful and build the) Tj T*
(habit of morality into the constitution of the race.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recognizing her intense feeling on moral lines, and seeing in her) Tj T*
(the rigidly preserved virtues of faith, submission, and) Tj T*
(self-sacrifice,?qualities which in the Dark Ages were held to be the) Tj T*
(first of virtues,?we have agreed of late years to call woman the) Tj T*
(moral superior of man. But the ceaseless growth of human life,) Tj T*
(social life, has developed in him new virtues, later, higher, more) Tj T*
(needful; and the moral nature of woman, as maintained in this) Tj T*
(rudimentary stage by her economic dependence, is a continual check) Tj T*
(to the progress of the human soul. The main feature of her life?the) Tj T*
(restriction of her range of duty to the love and service of her own) Tj T*
(immediate family?acts upon us continually as a retarding influence,) Tj T*
(hindering the expansion of the spirit of social love and service on) Tj T*
(which our very lives depend. It keeps the moral standard of the) Tj T*
(patriarchal era still before us, and blinds our eyes to the full) Tj T*
(duty of man.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An intense self-consciousness, born of the ceaseless contact of close) Tj T*
(personal relation; an inordinate self-interest, bred by the constant) Tj T*
(personal attention and service of this relation; a feverish, torturing,) Tj T*
(moral sensitiveness, without the width and clarity of vision of a) Tj T*
(full-grown moral sense; a thwarted will, used to meek surrender, cunning) Tj T*
(evasion, or futile rebellion; a childish, wavering, short-range) Tj T*
(judgment, handicapped by emotion; a measureless devotion to one?s own) Tj T*
(sex relatives, and a maternal passion swollen with the full strength of) Tj T*
(the great social heart, but denied social expression,?such psychic) Tj T*
(qualities as these, born in us all, are the inevitable result of the) Tj T*
(sexuo-economic relation.) Tj T*
ET
